message: "If you use FUSS in your research, please cite it using the following metadata."
type: software

title: "FUSS: Fourier Un-Steady Solver"

abstract: >-
  FUSS (Fourier Un-Steady Solver) is an open-source solid heat-conduction
  solver written in modern Fortran. It solves the steady-state and transient
  Fourier heat equation on multi-block structured grids using a cell-centred
  finite-volume formulation. FUSS supports multi-material domains,
  temperature-dependent thermal properties, volumetric heat sources, and
  mixed thermal boundary conditions, including prescribed temperature,
  heat flux, convection, and radiation. Its numerical capabilities include
  explicit time integration, implicit residual smoothing, local time
  stepping, grid sequencing, and multigrid acceleration. Parallel execution
  is supported through OpenMP and MPI, with output in Tecplot and VTK formats.

